  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The mirror",
  "description": "Use cones to set out two squares of about 5 × 5 metres that share one side (not to scale). Players work in pairs and one pair is active at a time. They stand in separate squares, facing each other. A leads and skates quickly between the cones in their square – forwards, backwards and sideways. B follows like a mirror image in the other square.\n\nChange pairs after about 10 seconds. Next time the pair is up, they swap roles.\n\nProgression: start without a puck, then with the stick on the ice, and finally with a puck.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep your eyes up so you see both the puck and your partner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Short, quick strides and bent knees make it easier to change direction."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Leader: vary the speed and direction – mix forward and backward skating."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Ask the players: which movement was easiest to follow, and which was hardest?"
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
